Main finding: `yoyo docs` reports success for crates and items that don't exist.
• `yoyo docs zzqq_definitely_not_a_crate_918` prints a green ✓, a docs.rs link and "Docs available at the URL above.", then exits 0. That link returns a 404.
• `yoyo docs serde NoSuchItemXyz` does the same thing.
• **Cause** (`src/docs.rs:15-33`): the fetch never checks the HTTP status. It only looks for three "not found" phrases in the page, and docs.rs now says "The requested crate does not exist", which matches none of them. So every missing page counts as found.
• **Tests:** the existing ones only check display text built from saved HTML. Nothing tests how a 404 is classified.
• **Why it's the top candidate:** users see it, the fix stays inside `src/docs.rs`, and it's outside dispatch. The trajectory warns that dispatch took 5 of the last 9 self-driven changes and says to put this session's self-driven slot somewhere else.

